  {
   "id": "q2",
   "number": "2",
   "type": "mcq_single",
   "stem": "The capacity of a glass is 200 m*l* and that of a bucket is 5*l*. How many glasses of water are needed to fill up the bucket ?",
   "options": [
    {
     "label": "A",
     "text": "15"
    },
    {
     "label": "B",
     "text": "20"
    },
    {
     "label": "C",
     "text": "25"
    },
    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "40"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "C",
   "solution": "(C) Capacity of a glass → 200 m*l*\n\nCapacity of a bucket = 5 *l* \\[1 *l* = 1000 m*l*\\] 5 *l* = 5 × 1000 m*l* = 5000 m*l*\n\nNo. of glasses of water requried\n\n= 5000 ÷ 200 = 25 glasses",
   "topics": [
    "Mathematics"
   ],
   "fields": {
    "Exam": "UIMO",
    "Class": 4,
    "Paper": "UIMO UM_SET_01",
    "Paper code": "UM_SET_01",
    "Section": "Mathematics"
   },
   "source": {
